{
  // Declaration-only build config. Emit settings, rootDir/outDir and the shared
  // exclude list all come from ../../tsconfig.build.base.json; what is local is
  // the entry list below. `server/passthrough.ts`, `server/forwarded.ts` and
  // `server/service.ts` are listed explicitly because each is its own subpath
  // entry — deliberately, so neither a passthrough-only app nor a
  // service-account consumer reaches the BFF handler graph — and an unlisted
  // entry emits no .d.ts at all.
  //
  // This package (with packages/api-errors, which runs the same generator) has
  // its own typescript pin: `catalog:tooling-tsc6` (6.0.3), against the
  // workspace's `tooling` catalog (7.0.2). The reason is the OpenAPI codegen — @hey-api/openapi-ts
  // builds the client by constructing AST nodes with the JS COMPILER API, which
  // the native 7.x compiler does not ship, so merely importing
  // openapi-ts.config.ts throws on 7.x. `generate` and the specs that import
  // that config therefore need a 6.x compiler. See the `tooling-tsc6` catalog in
  // pnpm-workspace.yaml, which is where the pin is edited and where the
  // fold-it-back-in condition is recorded.
  //
  // The generator's own peer range is permissive (`>=5.5.3 || >=6.0.0`), so the
  // pin is about what the compiler API ships, not about satisfying a peer.
  "extends": ["./tsconfig.json", "../../tsconfig.build.base.json"],
  "include": [
    "src/index.ts",
    "src/server/index.ts",
    "src/server/passthrough.ts",
    "src/server/forwarded.ts",
    "src/server/service.ts",
    "src/query/index.ts"
  ]
}
